# HR reference slice (golden path)

**Canonical reference:** `packages/features/hr-suite/src/employee-management/compliance-regulatory-tracking/`  
**Architecture trail:** `compliance-regulatory-tracking-architecture.md` (requirements + `## As-built summary` + per-code tables)  
**Companion rule:** `afenda-hr-feature-vertical` (folders, naming regex, export doors)

Do **not** re-invent layout from `@afenda/feature-system-admin` or legacy `@afenda/feature-hr` for new HR workbenches — **clone compliance**, rename domain.

## When this rule applies

- Implementing or extending any `employee-management/<capability>/` slice (e.g. `documents-management`).
- Adding `/hr/<section>` app adapters under `apps/erp/src/lib/hr-sections/`.
- Shipping governed lists/stats for HR (`surface/`, Pattern B + C).

Scaffold-only folders (placeholder `index.ts` only) may stay minimal until the slice ships.

## Seven layers (all required for a shipped slice)

| Layer | Owner | Pattern |
| ----- | ----- | ------- |
| 1. Schema & commands | `@afenda/db` | `hr-*.ts` modules; org-scoped windows; no DDL in feature package |
| 2. Access policy | `policies/hr.<domain>-access.policy.server.ts` | `requireHr*Read/Write`; optional sensitive capability (fail closed) |
| 3. Metadata registry | `surface/hr.<domain>-surface-metadata.shared.ts` | `*_LIST_SURFACE_KEYS`, search-param map, columns registry — **single source** |
| 4. Search params | `data/hr.<domain>-search-params.parse.shared.ts` | Parse URL → page-model input; every registry param maps to a model field (test it) |
| 5. Page model | `data/hr.<domain>.page-model.server.ts` | Parallel list loads; `settle*ListLoad` placeholders; call `build*ListSurface` from `surface/` only |
| 6. Governed UI | `surface/*.surface.ts` + `components/*-section.component.server.tsx` | Pattern B overview + Pattern C lists; trailing schemas accept **stored** statuses only |
| 7. App adapter | `apps/erp/src/lib/hr-sections/<slug>.server.tsx` | Guard once → `to*PageModelInput` → `build*PageModel` → workbench section; register in `manifest.shared.ts` |

Export doors: slice `server.ts` (I/O), `client.ts` (components), `metadata.ts` (keys, copy, parsers — **no tenant I/O**). Re-export from package `metadata.ts` / `server.ts`; **never** add long-lived stubs in package root `server.ts` for a shipped slice.

## Learnings to reuse (from compliance)

- **Derived vs stored status:** derive overdue/expiring/missing at read; Zod trailing schemas reject derived tokens on mutation; normalize to `pending` on write when needed.
- **Sensitive registers:** separate capability (e.g. `hr.<area>.sensitive.read`); mask in page model; document picker excludes restricted rows when false; mutations use `require*SensitiveWrite()`.
- **Registry-driven tests:** `compliance-workbench-metadata.test.ts`, `compliance-search-params.test.ts`, `compliance-list-eui-contract.test.ts` — add `<capability>-*` equivalents before marking shipped.
- **Architecture doc:** extend `*-architecture.md` with parent ARCH links, `## As-built summary`, HRM-* shipment matrix, per-requirement tables as code lands.
- **Cross-module boundaries:** vault/versioning in Document Management; obligation monitoring in Compliance — link by FK/readiness, do not duplicate storage UI.

## Promoting a new capability to “shipped”

1. Implement all seven layers under `src/employee-management/<capability>/`.
2. Add capability path to `SHIPPED_CAPABILITIES` in `packages/features/hr-suite/scripts/check-hr-feature-vertical-naming.mts` (pattern checks run automatically).
3. Register `hrSectionManifest` + `apps/erp/src/lib/hr-sections/<slug>.server.tsx` + route skeleton if new section.
4. Export slice from package `server.ts` / `metadata.ts` (remove root-level `denied()` stubs for that area).
5. Run verification (below) and update architecture shipment matrix.

## Anti-patterns

| Avoid | Use instead |
| ----- | ----------- |
| List `*.surface.ts` under `data/` | `surface/` bucket |
| Full dataset to client for pagination | Server window + `GovernedPatternCListSection` |
| Audit strings in `contracts/` | `events/*.event.ts` |
| Client importing `@afenda/db` | `./server` actions + page model |
| Hand-written DDL in feature package | `packages/db/src/schema` → `pnpm db:generate` → `pnpm db:migrate` |
| Shipping without `## As-built summary` in architecture md | Same PR as first real UI |

## Verification

```bash
pnpm exec tsx packages/features/hr-suite/scripts/check-hr-feature-vertical-naming.mts
pnpm --filter @afenda/feature-hr-suite test
pnpm architecture:check
pnpm lint:governed-renderers   # when surfaces/registry change
```

